\title{SVDMx: child or child/adult mortality-indexed mortality schedules}
\description{
Implementation of the SVD-Comp mortality model. The \code{qx()} function generates full age schedules of mortality in
single year or 5-year age groups from either child mortality, 5q0, alone or both child, 5q0, and adult mortality, 45q15.
For a full description of the model see arXiv preprint Clark (2016) \doi{doi:10.48550/arXiv.1612.01408} and published paper in
Clark (2019) \doi{doi:10.1007/s13524-019-00785-3}.
}
\section{SVDMx functions}{

\strong{qx} takes child or child/adult mortality and generates full age schedules of mortality.

\strong{plotqx} plots the schedules generated by \code{qx()} on the natural or logit scale, and saves the plot as a PNG or PDF file if asked.

\strong{q1to5} converts single-year 1qx to five-year 5qx.

\strong{lifetable} makes complete life tables, abridged or single-year, from the same inputs as \code{qx()}; \strong{lifetableBatch} makes a batch of them from a file of inputs; and \strong{writeLifetables} writes them to Excel, CSV, fixed-column text or JSON files.
}

\section{Calibrations}{

The models are calibrated on successive versions of the Human Mortality Database: \code{mods2018} (the
models in the \emph{Demography} paper), \code{mods2021}, \code{mods2022}, \code{mods2024}, \code{mods2025},
and \code{mods2026} (the default). Choose one with the \code{modsv} argument of \code{qx()}.
}

